  "source": "# Semantics: the (any) binding passthrough reduces to the ONE plain\n# shape on every engine (parsanol-ruby#383) — scalars and capture\n# leaves as their text, named groups as string-keyed plain hashes.\ngrammar AnyBinding version \"1.0.0\" edition 2 {\n  word = 1*( %x41-5A / %x61-7A )\n  digit = %x30-39\n  dash = \"-\"\n  number = ( word ) as name\n  suffix = ( dash ( 1*( digit ) ) as num )\n  identifier = number suffix\n  entry identifier: identifier\n  bindings identifier {\n    name -> name (any)\n    num -> num (any)\n  }\n  test {\n    accept \"ABC-12\"\n  }\n}\n",
